---
/**
 * The kind of gata Hakop makes.
 *
 * This page exists because "gata" names more than one pastry, and somebody
 * who grew up with the flat stamped round will order the wrong thing if the
 * difference is buried three headings down a long explainer. It is its own
 * URL so it can be sent to one person as one link. See docs/DECISIONS.md
 * D-008.
 *
 * The rules that hold on every page about the food hold here. Ingredient
 * names are public and legally required. Amounts, ratios, timings and method
 * are the recipe, and they never enter this repository.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Explainer from "./_Explainer.astro";
import pan from "@/assets/photos/gata-tray-full.jpg";
---

<Explainer
  slug="rolled-and-sliced"
  seoTitle="The rolled and sliced kind of gata"
  description="There is more than one kind of gata. Hakop's is the rolled and sliced kind: nut filling turned inside the dough, cut across into pieces and scattered with sesame."
>
  <div class="prose-col rolled__body">
    <p>
      The filling is turned inside the dough rather than layered on top of it:
      the dough goes around a sweet nut filling as a long log, and the log is
      cut across into pieces. The tops are washed with egg and scattered with
      sesame, and that egg wash is what makes them gold.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is more than one kind of gata. Hakop's is this one, the rolled and
      sliced kind. It is not the flat stamped round that some families make,
      and the two are different enough that it is worth saying so before
      anybody is disappointed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The sesame goes on by hand, thrown rather than pressed into a pattern,
      which is why no two pieces are marked the same way. It is sold by the
      tray rather than by the piece.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="rolled__figure">
    <Image
      src={pan}
      alt="A whole sheet pan of gata, every piece egg washed to a deep gold and scattered with sesame seeds."
      width={1060}
      height={1180}
      widths={[400, 640, 1060]}
      sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 26rem, 88vw"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <figcaption>Every piece on the pan is a slice off the same log.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</Explainer>

<style>
  .rolled__body {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .rolled__figure {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    max-width: 26rem;
  }

  .rolled__figure :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .rolled__figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-crust-soft);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }
</style>
